{"p":{"slug":"pedro-costa","first":"Pedro","last":"Costa","cc":"POR","iso":"pt","country":"Portugal","g":0,"img":"https://platform.worldofsailors.com/storage/uploads/2026/03/11-pedro-costa-7-1772976912.webp","club":"Clube We Do Sailing","clubs":["Clube We Do Sailing"],"cm":170,"kg":75,"bio":"At the age of 6 I started sailing in the Optimist Class and at the age of 16 I started my journey on the 420, with my brother, Diogo Costa. We became National Champions of this Class, in 2015 and 2016, and in addition to many other regattas, we were also National Champions of Match Racing sub23 and World Champions 2016.\nI have had this passion for sailing since a very early age and I intend to continue to follow this Sport.\nDespite the fact that the Class 470 Men was eliminated from the Olympic Games, I have ambitions to participate in more Olympic Games. So I had to choose another Class, the 49er. In which I am currently as a skipper and as expected it's a big change, both personally and technically, but I'm doing my best in this New Challenge in order to pursue my dream.","soc":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/pedroeuricocosta/","facebook":"https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=1720705700"},"rk":{"s":[38327,5.38,38122,"2026-11-24",[6428,"2024-11-12"]],"c":[2514,366.8,1911,"2026-11-24",[31,"2021-03-16"]]},"st":{"ev":90,"win":4,"pod":16,"avg":4.2,"best":1},"cls":["ILCA 6 (Open)","49er","ILCA 4","470 (Men)","470 (Mixte)","J/70"],"recn":2},"res":{"s":[["2025-08-31","Cascais Vela 2025","Cascais","POR","SB20","Local",3,15,2.5,6],["2025-07-06","Mirpuri Foundation Sailing Trophy 2025","Cascais","POR","SB20","Local",2,29,2.9,3],["2024-06-23","Campeonato Nacional SB20 2024","Cascais","POR","SB20","National",9,12,0,8],["2024-04-27","Semaine Olympique Française Hyères 2024","Hyeres","FRA","49er","International",21,185,0,16],["2024-04-06","53 Trofeo S.A.R Princesa Sofia / World Cup Series","Mallorca","ESP","49er","International",70,557,0,15],["2024-02-25","6th Portugal Grand Pri